        <item>
            <title>2.27.0</title>
            <pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 01:11:22 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>110</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.27.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features

- **Japanese bold text now renders as bold.** CommonMark only lets a `**` close a span when the closing marker is right-flanking, and Japanese prose puts no space after punctuation — so `**注意。**次` could not close, and both markers showed up as literal asterisks. Canopy now repairs the markup on its way to the chat view, moving the punctuation outside the span (`**注意**。次`). The opener fails the same way on `は**「引用」**を`, and that end is repaired too.

  Measured against 25,264 Japanese assistant messages from real transcripts, rendered with the same Markdown engine the chat view uses: messages showing a literal `**` went from 1,701 to 37, with none made worse and every message keeping exactly the characters it started with.

  The repair runs while a reply streams in and when a session's history is replayed, and it leaves code alone — fenced blocks, inline code and link destinations pass through untouched, and only non-ASCII punctuation is ever moved, so a link's `)` or an HTML tag's `>` stays where it was.

  Set `CANOPY_DISABLE_CJK_EMPHASIS_REPAIR=1` to turn it off.
]]></description>
